Help Scout is an email-first help desk platform providing shared inboxes, live chat, knowledge bases, and a customer portal [1][2].

Developers authenticate API requests using OAuth 2.0 [3]. Access is self-serve, provided via a freemium model that includes a free trial [1][2]. The API surface includes a REST API (v2) and webhooks [1][3]. Official MCP support is currently unknown [1][4].

Integration is straightforward for developers familiar with OAuth 2.0 flows, but it requires managing short-lived (two-day) access tokens and implementing refresh logic [3]. The primary blocker is the rate-limiting system, which is plan-tiered and shared across an account; additionally, write requests (POST, PUT, PATCH, DELETE) consume double the quota of read requests [3][5].

```
// Example: Requesting an access token via client_credentials
const tokenResponse = await axios.post('https://api.helpscout.net/v2/oauth2/token', {
  grant_type: 'client_credentials',
  client_id: clientId,
  client_secret: clientSecret
});

// Example: Authenticated request header
headers: { 'Authorization': `Bearer ${accessToken}` }
```
